# P02 experiments and proof review

Rerun capability laboratory, ablations, bridges_phase and validation in a fresh output directory, plus the independent oracle_contract_check. Verify 270 small Deutsch preparations,56 DJ operator coordinates,62 source BV strings,132 UNIQUE-SAT promises,192 primitive eigenvectors and Walsh n1..6 ranks. Keep the 65,535-state Simon/36-oracle result in its n2,no-ancilla,one-query scope. The extra oracle checker covers 552 degenerate-oracle matrices,4 Deutsch functions and 126 standard-XOR BV secrets; it illustrates but does not prove arbitrary-query no-information behavior.

Analytic review is more important than larger finite enumeration. Independently check: the w=0 Deutsch case; secret independence of preparation/gates; the three-balanced DJ relation; degree preservation through each query and secret-independent map; complete adaptive branching as an injective direct-sum instrument; variable stopping times; the strict monomial-count inequality forq<n; and informative-interface upper bounds. An incomplete or postselected instrument is a different model, not a harmless proof shortcut.

Useful new work: an exact small-q DJ solver with frozen dimension/gate/readout restrictions can sharpen examples, but cannot authorize an arbitrary-ancilla optimum without proof. A broader Simon theorem would need new analytic work. Neither is necessary to start the current scoped draft.

No timing experiment is needed to prove a query bound. Do not replace query complexity with runtime for dense state-vector simulation. UNIQUE-SAT remains one query plus O(n) other operations, with the original source credited.
